2004.11.04.ET:

Be sure to review the online page,

http://eyegene.ophthy.med.umich.edu/SoftwareRegistration/features.php

for the latest changes in the development version of the program.

Version 0.936 is a bug fix release with a few additional and significant
features.  The main improvements are:

* C++ STL Containers: 

    Many more features of C++ and the C++ Standard Template Library (STL)
    are now present in the code base in order to provide for better memory
    management and reduce bugs.  A number of show-stopping segmentation faults
    have been eliminated by changing over to use STL containers 
    in several important places in the code.

* Command Log:

    In addition to madeline.log, madeline.dtl, and madeline.err, Madeline 
    version 0.936 now produces a fourth log which records the commands that 
    have been entered by the user. The default name of this log file is 
    "madeline.cmd". This new log file simplifies the process of creating a 
    script file that can be executed using the run command.

* Smart Table Selection:

    Users often inadvertently attempt to open up the ASCII/UTF-8 data file 
    directly instead of using the .mfh file generated by the recognize command. 

    With the smart table selection implemented in version 0.936, the program now 
    senses when you attempt to open up an ASCII/UTF-8 table and automatically looks 
    for a matching .mfh file to open instead. If the .mfh file is not found, the 
    program now automatically runs recognize for you and then opens the .mfh file. 

    Smart table selection is now present on the following commands: OPEN, LOAD, 
    GRAPH OPEN, GRAPH LOAD, READ, and COMPOSE. Smart table selection is not present on 
    the MERGE command as this command in particular requires the user to carefully 
    check the formatting of files to be merged together. 

    The implementation of smart table selection has also eliminated the occurrence of
    show-stopping segmentation faults when attempting to open up a file in the wrong
    format.


